# the slice engine on track 3: picked from SEL's list (ENGINE: slice, its first preset "breaks", the track
# off the conductor), the classic break cut in eight. Written on the steps a slice every two steps (F3 = slice 1
# .. C4 = slice 8) it plays the break straight; then re-sequenced; the same at 90 BPM (the slices follow the
# tempo); "jungle" (16 slices, mono) on a sixteenth pattern; the keys by hand; the picture with the slice playing.
# WAVs of each (tools/slice_renders.sh copies them into build/slice_renders/ with an index).
wait 300
spin ALGO 2
expect trk 3
tap EDIT
expect page Engine
tap SEL
turn ALGO 6 30
tap SEL
expect par3.0 7
expect par3.1 12
expect par3.2 1
expect par3.brain 0
wait 60
shot slice_engine.png
# the break straight: slice k on step 2k - 1
step 3 1 1 53
step 3 1 3 54
step 3 1 5 55
step 3 1 7 56
step 3 1 9 57
step 3 1 11 58
step 3 1 13 59
step 3 1 15 60
wav slice_straight.wav
tap PLAY
wait 1150
shot slice_playing.png
wait 2850
tap PLAY
wait 400
wavstop
# re-sequenced: kick, kick, snare, ghost, the double kick, snare, the open hat
step 3 1 1 53
step 3 1 3 53
step 3 1 5 55
step 3 1 7 54
step 3 1 9 58
step 3 1 11 57
step 3 1 13 55
step 3 1 14 56
step 3 1 15 60
step 3 1 16 59
wav slice_resequenced.wav
tap PLAY
wait 4000
tap PLAY
wait 400
wavstop
# the same at 90 BPM: each slice longer, the break still a bar
bpm 90
wait 20
expect tempo 90
wav slice_resequenced_90.wav
tap PLAY
wait 5333
tap PLAY
wait 400
wavstop
bpm 120
# jungle: sixteen slices, mono (each note cuts the last), on every sixteenth
turn PRESET 4
expect par3.2 2
expect par3.5 1
wait 60
shot slice_chop.png
step 3 1 1 53
step 3 1 2 53
step 3 1 3 55
step 3 1 4 54
step 3 1 5 57
step 3 1 6 58
step 3 1 7 53
step 3 1 8 60
step 3 1 9 61
step 3 1 10 61
step 3 1 11 63
step 3 1 12 64
step 3 1 13 57
step 3 1 14 66
step 3 1 15 67
step 3 1 16 68
wav slice_chop.wav
tap PLAY
wait 4000
tap PLAY
wait 400
wavstop
# the keys by hand: the white keys from F3 play slices 1, 3, 5 ... of eight (breaks again)
turn PRESET -1
expect par3.2 1
wav slice_keys.wav
tapkey w0
wait 250
tapkey w1
wait 250
key w2 down
wait 100
shot slice_key_held.png
wait 150
key w2 up
tapkey w3
wait 250
tapkey b0
wait 250
tapkey b1
wait 500
wavstop
# the knobs: 32 slices, a short gate, pitch down; then an empty user slot
spin K2 3
spin K4 -80
spin K3 -12
expect par3.2 3
expect par3.3 52
wait 40
shot slice_knobs.png
tap SEL
wait 40
shot slice_list.png
tap HOME
param 3 1 9
wait 40
shot slice_empty.png
listen
where
said slice
